1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,042
Hello, and thank you for asking me to your teachers' meeting to talk about the Dinosaur Museum

2
00:00:05,042 --> 00:00:09,490
and to tell you a bit about what you can do with your students there.

3
00:00:09,490 --> 00:00:13,800
Well, let me give you some of the basic information first.

4
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,612
In regard to opening hours,

5
00:00:15,612 --> 00:00:22,060
we're open every day of the week from 9.00 am to 8.00 pm except on Mondays

6
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:24,670
when we close at 1.30 pm.

7
00:00:24,670 --> 00:00:29,800
And, in fact the only day in the year when we're closed is on the 25th of December.

8
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:35,030
You can book a guided tour for your school group any time that we're open.

9
00:00:35,030 --> 00:00:37,929
If you bring a school group to the museum,

10
00:00:37,929 --> 00:00:42,760
when you arrive we ask you to remain with your group in the car park.

11
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:46,440
One or more of the tour guides will welcome you there

12
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:49,260
and brief you about what the tour will be about.

13
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:52,889
We do this there because our entrance is quite small

14
00:00:52,889 --> 00:00:57,970
and we really haven't got much room for briefing groups in the exhibition area.

15
00:00:57,970 --> 00:01:01,591
As far as the amount of time you'll need goes,

16
00:01:01,591 --> 00:01:08,470
if you bring a school group you should plan on allowing a minimum of 90 minutes for the visit.

17
00:01:08,470 --> 00:01:13,358
This allows 15 minutes to get on and off the coach,

18
00:01:13,358 --> 00:01:18,690
45 minutes for the guided tour and 30 minutes for after-tour activities.

19
00:01:18,690 --> 00:01:22,900
If you're going to have lunch at the museum you will

20
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:24,860
of course, have to allow more time.

21
00:01:24,860 --> 00:01:29,800
There are two cafes in the museum, with seating for 80 people.

22
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:33,960
If you want to eat there you'll need to reserve some seating

23
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:36,810
as they can get quite crowded at lunch time.

24
00:01:36,810 --> 00:01:39,982
Then outside the museum at the back there are tables,

25
00:01:39,982 --> 00:01:44,740
and students can bring their own lunch and eat it there in the open air.

26
00:01:44,740 --> 00:01:51,942
When the students come into the museum foyer we ask them to check in their backpacks with their books,

27
00:01:51,942 --> 00:01:56,490
lunch boxes, etc, at the cloakroom before they enter the museum proper.

28
00:01:56,490 --> 00:02:01,620
I'm afraid in the past we have had a few things gone missing after school visits

29
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:03,640
so this is a strict rule.

30
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:07,180
Also, some of the exhibits are fragile

31
00:02:07,180 --> 00:02:10,000
and we don't want them to be accidentally knocked.

32
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,430
But we do provide school students with handouts with questions and quizzes on them.

33
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:19,060
There's so much that students can learn in the museum

34
00:02:19,060 --> 00:02:21,650
and it's fun for them to have something to do.

35
00:02:21,650 --> 00:02:25,600
Of course they'll need to bring something to write with for these.

36
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:29,200
We do allow students to take photographs.

37
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:37,330
For students who are doing projects it's useful to make some kind of visual record of what they see that they can add to their reports.

38
00:02:37,330 --> 00:02:42,620
And finally, they should not bring anything to eat into the museum

39
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:44,360
or drinks of any kind.

40
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:49,400
There are also a few things the students can do after the tour.

41
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:55,800
In the theatrette on the ground floor there are continuous screenings of short documentaries about dinosaurs

42
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:58,600
which they can see at any time.

43
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:04,814
We used to have an activity room with more interactive things like making models of dinosaurs

44
00:03:04,814 --> 00:03:08,698
and drawing and painting pictures, even hunting for dinosaur eggs,

45
00:03:08,698 --> 00:03:13,880
but unfortunately the room was damaged in a bad storm recently

46
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:15,300
when water came in the roof,

47
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:17,630
so that's closed at the moment.

48
00:03:17,630 --> 00:03:20,240
But we do have an IT centre

49
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:25,060
where students have access to CD ROMs with a range of dinosaur games.

50
00:03:25,060 --> 00:03:27,760
These games are a lot of fun

51
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:32,016
but they also teach the students about the lives of dinosaurs,

52
00:03:32,016 --> 00:03:37,040
how they found food, protected their habitat, survived threats, that kind of thing.

53
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:40,880
And... I think that's all I have to tell you.

54
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:46,040
Please feel free to ask any questions if you would like to know anything else...
